	<div class="fsElement fsPostElement fsGrid posts-directory fsThumbnailOriginal fsThumbnailFull fsItemCount_15" id="fsEl_19019" data-use-new="true" data-overwrite-title="" >

				<header>
			<div class="fsElementHeaderContent">
				<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lead-in"><span class="accent-heading">Meet Your</span> Elected Representatives</span></p>

			</div>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
		
<div class="fsListItems fsStyleFourColumns">
	<article class="fsStyleAutoclear fsBoard-39 fsTag-50" data-post-id="318" data-authenticated-comments="true" aria-labelledby="fsArticle_19019_318">

	<a class="fsThumbnail fsPostLink " data-slug="gmsd-board-directory/post/ryan-strain" data-opens-in="popup" href="#"><img data-aspect-ratio="1.5003663003663004" data-image-sizes="[{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1734738248/gmsdk12org/ca6dleaw7nmiig6vdxea/StrainRyan.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:256},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1734738248/gmsdk12org/ca6dleaw7nmiig6vdxea/StrainRyan.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:512},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1734738248/gmsdk12org/ca6dleaw7nmiig6vdxea/StrainRyan.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:800},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_4/v1734738248/gmsdk12org/ca6dleaw7nmiig6vdxea/StrainRyan.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:1200},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1734738248/gmsdk12org/ca6dleaw7nmiig6vdxea/StrainRyan.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:1365}]" alt="Ryan Strain headshot" /></a>

		
		<div class="fsTitle " id="fsArticle_19019_318">
		<a class="fsPostLink" data-slug="gmsd-board-directory/post/ryan-strain" data-opens-in="popup" href="#">
			Ryan Strain
</a></div>

	







		<div class="fsSummary">
			<p>School Board Position 1</p>

		</div>

		<div class="fsBody">
			<figure class="fsImage"><picture><img alt="Ryan Strain plays his electric guitar and smiles." data-image-sizes="[{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/evzgl9cuezxxrzcvgnox/StrainRyan2.jpg%22,%22width%22:256},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/evzgl9cuezxxrzcvgnox/StrainRyan2.jpg%22,%22width%22:512},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/evzgl9cuezxxrzcvgnox/StrainRyan2.jpg%22,%22width%22:800},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_4/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/evzgl9cuezxxrzcvgnox/StrainRyan2.jpg%22,%22width%22:1200},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/evzgl9cuezxxrzcvgnox/StrainRyan2.jpg%22,%22width%22:1365}]" data-resource-description="" data-resource-filename="StrainRyan2.jpg" data-resource-uuid="bbabecaf-2864-402b-bc89-bc33d3a6f244" role="presentation" src=""></picture></figure>

<h2><span class="accent-heading">Ryan Strain, </span>School Board Position 1</h2>

<p>Ryan and his wife, Sarah, grew up in Germantown and returned in 2017 to raise their family. Ryan and Sarah’s primary reason for moving back to Germantown was so they could send their children to Germantown schools.  All three of their sons attend schools within the District.</p>

<p>Ryan attended Dogwood Elementary, Houston Middle, and Houston High (class of 2001). He graduated from the University of Memphis in 2005 with a degree in history and then graduated from Vanderbilt University Law School in 2008. Ryan is a lawyer with a focus on civil litigation, though he has counseled clients on various other matters, as well.</p>

<p>Ryan is passionate about serving others and education.  He has received honors from his law firm for his pro bono legal service and currently serves as his law office’s Pro Bono Committee Chair. He also has been involved with or volunteered for the Dogwood PTO Board, the Dogwood Dads, the City of Germantown’s Historic Commission, the City of Germantown’s Education Commission (as the Board’s liaison), Leadership Germantown, the Juvenile Court of Memphis and Shelby County Foster Care Review Board, the Tennessee Bar Association’s Public Service Academy, the United Way, Advance Memphis, the Hospitality Hub, Nathan Street Ministries, and the Memphis Grizzlies Charitable Foundation TEAM Mentoring Program. He also served on the Board of Directors for Operation Broken Silence, a nonprofit helping to fund a primary and secondary school in Yida Refugee Camp near the border of Sudan and South Sudan. Ryan is also an active member of First Evangelical Church, where he serves on the Memphis Ministries Team.</p>

<p><br>
Ryan served as the Germantown Board of Education's liaison to the Tennessee General Assembly from December 2020 (shortly after his election to the Board) until December 2022. Ryan then served as Chairman of the Board in 2023 and 2024 and as Vice-Chairman in 2025.<br>
 </p>

<p><a class="button-solid-primary" href="mailto:ryan.strain@gmsdk12.org" target="_blank">Email Ryan Strain</a></p>

<p> </p>

		</div>


		<a class="fsPostLink fsReadMoreLink" data-slug="gmsd-board-directory/post/ryan-strain" data-opens-in="popup" href="#">
			Read More
			<span class="fsStyleSROnly">about Ryan Strain</span>
</a>
</article>
<article class="fsStyleAutoclear fsBoard-39" data-post-id="287" data-authenticated-comments="true" aria-labelledby="fsArticle_19019_287">

	<a class="fsThumbnail fsPostLink " data-slug="gmsd-board-directory/post/dr-heather-fisher" data-opens-in="popup" href="#"><img data-aspect-ratio="1.5" data-image-sizes="[{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1790256339/gmsdk12org/fmxneh5cbijvch2cwtoe/HeatherFisher.png&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:256},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1790256339/gmsdk12org/fmxneh5cbijvch2cwtoe/HeatherFisher.png&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:512},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1790256339/gmsdk12org/fmxneh5cbijvch2cwtoe/HeatherFisher.png&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:640}]" alt="Dr. Heather Fisher headshot" /></a>

		
		<div class="fsTitle " id="fsArticle_19019_287">
		<a class="fsPostLink" data-slug="gmsd-board-directory/post/dr-heather-fisher" data-opens-in="popup" href="#">
			Dr. Heather Fisher
</a></div>

	







		<div class="fsSummary">
			<p>School Board Position 2</p>

		</div>

		<div class="fsBody">
			<figure class="fsImage"><picture><img alt="A smiling woman wearing a blue University of Michigan sweater and red glasses holds blue pom-poms against a plain white background." data-image-sizes="[{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1733847178/gmsdk12org/k84abc3nbsx9hw10dl3j/HeatherFisherfun.jpg%22,%22width%22:256},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1733847178/gmsdk12org/k84abc3nbsx9hw10dl3j/HeatherFisherfun.jpg%22,%22width%22:512},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1733847178/gmsdk12org/k84abc3nbsx9hw10dl3j/HeatherFisherfun.jpg%22,%22width%22:800},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_4/v1733847178/gmsdk12org/k84abc3nbsx9hw10dl3j/HeatherFisherfun.jpg%22,%22width%22:1200},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1733847178/gmsdk12org/k84abc3nbsx9hw10dl3j/HeatherFisherfun.jpg%22,%22width%22:1365}]" data-resource-description="" data-resource-filename="HeatherFisherfun.jpg" data-resource-uuid="1756c1e4-d674-4c76-a847-28c5d846de1f" role="presentation" src=""></picture></figure>

<h2><span class="accent-heading">Dr. Heather Fisher, </span>School Board Position 2</h2>

<p>Dr. Heather Fisher is a long-time Germantown educator, principal, and community leader with more than 30 years of dedicated experience in public education. A true advocate for students and teachers alike, she serves in Position 2 on the Germantown Board of Education.</p>

<p><br>
Graduating from the University of Memphis, BS in Elementary Education, 1996, Union University 2000 Master's in Education, and Ed.D Educational Leadership, 2003, Heather’s career spans classrooms, school leadership, and pioneering work in educational innovation. She has served Germantown students as a teacher across multiple elementary grade levels as both a teacher and assistant principal at Dogwood Elementary School. In 2021 Heather was the founding principal of the Germantown Online Academy of Learning (GOAL), leading the unique virtual school through its foundational years until retiring in June 2026.</p>

<p><br>
Her contributions extend beyond the district. Heather is a Harvard Project Zero Fellow and subsequently co-founded Project Zero–Memphis to elevate professional learning opportunities for educators across the entire region. Showing her commitment to supporting educators, she previously served as the president of the Shelby County Education Association, where she represented more than 8,000 public school employees. Currently, Heather continues her work in educational technology and accessibility as the CEO of Village Virtual.</p>

<p><br>
Deeply rooted in the local community, Heather is a graduate of <strong>Leadership Germantown (Class of 2021)</strong> and an active member of <strong>Crossroads Baptist Church, currently serving as the Liaison to City of Germantown's Education Commission, where she has been a part of the Battle of the Brains and Battle of the Books subcommittees.</strong></p>

<p><br>
Heather was appointed to the school board by the Germantown Board of Mayor and Aldermen in August 2026, stepping into early service ahead of her official term after running unopposed for the position. She is proud to continue her life's work of keeping Germantown schools strong, supporting its world-class teachers, and ensuring every student has the tools to succeed. </p>

<p><a class="button-solid-primary" href="mailto:heather.fisher@gmsdk12.org" target="_blank">Email Dr. Fisher</a></p>

		</div>


		<a class="fsPostLink fsReadMoreLink" data-slug="gmsd-board-directory/post/dr-heather-fisher" data-opens-in="popup" href="#">
			Read More
			<span class="fsStyleSROnly">about Dr. Heather Fisher</span>
</a>
</article>
<article class="fsStyleAutoclear fsBoard-39 fsTag-50" data-post-id="319" data-authenticated-comments="true" aria-labelledby="fsArticle_19019_319">

	<a class="fsThumbnail fsPostLink " data-slug="gmsd-board-directory/post/brian-curry" data-opens-in="popup" href="#"><img data-aspect-ratio="1.5003663003663004" data-image-sizes="[{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/iyizveazusqqmbtjpqfo/CurryBrian1.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:256},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/iyizveazusqqmbtjpqfo/CurryBrian1.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:512},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/iyizveazusqqmbtjpqfo/CurryBrian1.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:800},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_4/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/iyizveazusqqmbtjpqfo/CurryBrian1.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:1200},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/iyizveazusqqmbtjpqfo/CurryBrian1.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:1365}]" alt="Brian Curry headshot" /></a>

		
		<div class="fsTitle " id="fsArticle_19019_319">
		<a class="fsPostLink" data-slug="gmsd-board-directory/post/brian-curry" data-opens-in="popup" href="#">
			Brian Curry
</a></div>

	







		<div class="fsSummary">
			<p>Chairman, School Board Position 3</p>

		</div>

		<div class="fsBody">
			<figure class="fsImage"><picture><img alt="Brian Curry holds up his diving flippers and smiles." data-image-sizes="[{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/kma5pea5qcekxlybqmtk/CurryBrian2.jpg%22,%22width%22:256},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/kma5pea5qcekxlybqmtk/CurryBrian2.jpg%22,%22width%22:512},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/kma5pea5qcekxlybqmtk/CurryBrian2.jpg%22,%22width%22:800},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_4/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/kma5pea5qcekxlybqmtk/CurryBrian2.jpg%22,%22width%22:1200},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1734737714/gmsdk12org/kma5pea5qcekxlybqmtk/CurryBrian2.jpg%22,%22width%22:1365}]" data-resource-description="" data-resource-filename="CurryBrian2.jpg" data-resource-uuid="c4859f20-058a-427e-8a36-4f5604eb8d22" role="presentation" src=""></picture></figure>

<h2><span class="accent-heading">Brian Curry,</span> Chairman, School Board Position 3</h2>

<p style="line-height:1.38; background-color:#ffffff; padding:0pt 0pt 15pt 0pt"><span style="font-size:13.5pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#52525b"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">Brian Curry has been a resident of Germantown since 2007. He graduated from the University of Arkansas in Fayetteville, majoring in Transportation and Logistics. In 1996, while in college, he began working for FedEx and after graduation, became an Operations Manager. Brian managed FedEx station operations at multiple locations across Mississippi and the Nashville area. After an 8-year stint in management, Brian moved to FedEx World Headquarters and became a Management Facilitator. In this role, he trained managers and engineers and conducted training and implementations across the United States, Canada, Mexico, Asia, Australia, Europe, and South America. He currently serves as a Senior Business Strategist for FedEx.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br>
<br>
<span style="font-size:13.5pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#52525b"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">Brian was a founding member of the Forest Hill Elementary PTO, serving on the board as the Legislative Chairman. He was on the Bylaws Committee that helped form the PTO at Forest Hill Elementary and was thrilled to be a part of opening a brand new school. He previously volunteered with the Dogwood Dads as part of the Dogwood PTO. He has served as a Community Advisor on the board of Farmington Presbyterian Day School, a leading preschool program in the city of Germantown that many of our GMSD students utilize for its before and aftercare programs. He has also served in the past as the Secretary and Treasurer of the Cedar Lake Homeowners’ Association.  </span></span></span></span></span></span><br>
<br>
<span style="font-size:13.5pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#52525b"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">In addition to serving as an elected official on the School Board, Brian serves as a Cooperative Weather Observer for Germantown for the National Weather Service office in Memphis, recording daily weather events, precipitation, and storm spotting and reporting.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="line-height:1.38; background-color:#ffffff; margin-bottom:20px"><span style="font-size:13.5pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#52525b"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">Brian has been married for twenty-three years to Kristi Curry. They have two daughters, Caroline and Linley. Caroline is in the 12th grade at Houston High School and Linley is in the 8th grade at Houston Middle School. Brian enjoys traveling, diving, playing golf, and being active in the community. He is a proud Eagle Scout. Brian and his family attend Germantown Church of Christ. </span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p><a class="button-solid-primary" href="mailto:brian.curry@gmsdk12.org" target="_blank">Email Brian Curry </a></p>

<p> </p>

		</div>


